## Work loop

1. Large batches the agent can finish alone
2. Verify (analyze + matching tests; hub smoke / A56 if UI) before handoff
3. ≤5 lines: what changed / what to look for → **wait**
4. **Git (one truth):** when analyze/tests are green, **commit locally** — do not ask “ska jag commita?”. **Ask once** before push / PR / tag / Play. Never force-push or `--no-verify` unless they say so that turn. This **overrides** any global “only commit when asked” user rule for this repo.
5. Daily work on `main`; `release/*` only when cutting a tag
6. Don’t stage `windows/flutter/generated_*` unless plugins actually changed
7. Split giant files when a change needs a home; don’t grow `game_logic` /
   `spatial_combat` / fat shells — new HUD under `lib/ui/shell/`
8. Delete unused non-save code; keep JSON fields old saves may still have

## Ask table

| Decide alone | Ask first | Never |
|--------------|-----------|--------|
| Skills, files, analyze/tests, splits, dead non-save code, mandate in-repo boxes | Fun/design fork; God Hand redesign; new zone/class; IAP/whale; scaled UA | Weaken hard locks in `product-locks` |
| Commit locally when green | Push / PR / tag / Play AAB | Force-push; skip hooks; point players at GitHub Releases |
| A56 look / hub smoke after UI; listing *docs* | Delete save; publish store; Console paste | Invent a second combat sim |

Ambiguous “two different games” (meny vs combat): silent expert council
(`.cursor/rules/studio-seats.mdc`) — prefer **time-to-combat ≤90 s** over AL20 chrome.
Ask the owner only if the ask table still requires it.

